          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/batch-processing/spark-metastore-catalog/#external-schema-registries">External schema registries (for streaming/Avro)</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Confluent/AWS Glue Schema Registry stores Avro/Protobuf schemas centrally so streaming producers and Spark consumers can validate and evolve schemas independently.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/batch-processing/spark-metastore-catalog/#catalog-namespace-isolation">Catalog namespace isolation</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Multiple catalogs/databases isolate table namespaces (catalog.database.table) so different teams or environments don't collide on table names.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/batch-processing/spark-metastore-catalog/#table-discovery-and-metadata-sync">Table discovery and metadata sync</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Crawlers (e.g. Glue Crawler) or MSCK REPAIR TABLE scan storage to detect new partitions/files and sync metastore metadata with what's actually on disk.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li class="rm-index-group">
        <h3 class="rm-index-heading"><a href="/level-3-technologies/batch-processing/spark-lakehouse-formats/">Lakehouse Table Formats</a></h3>
