          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/batch-processing/spark-data-quality/#schema-enforcement-and-evolution-policies">Schema enforcement and evolution policies</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Rejecting or auto-adapting to unexpected incoming schema changes — controlled per table via mode settings like failOnSchemaMismatch or mergeSchema.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/batch-processing/spark-data-quality/#data-lineage-verification">Data lineage verification</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Tracking which upstream sources and transformations produced a given dataset, used to trace root causes when downstream data quality issues appear.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-3-technologies/batch-processing/spark-data-quality/#pipeline-alerting-on-quality-metrics">Pipeline alerting on quality metrics</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Wiring quality check failures (from Deequ, Great Expectations, or custom checks) into alerting systems so pipelines fail loudly instead of shipping bad data silently.</span></li>
